  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: The only completed experiment (config_014: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) yields ~48.5% validation accuracy, giving a single baseline but leaving the central question of the study unanswered—does adding image information improve multimodal cellular profiling? Uncertainty: We have no data on whether image features contribute any signal, making it impossible to prioritize among the many multimodal configurations. Question tested: config_006 keeps the RNA encoder (pca_n2000), profile setting (singleprofile), and aggregation (none) identical to config_014, adding only an imagenet_vit_l image encoder and a simple concat fusion. This isolates the effect of the image modality with minimal confounds. Why this is the best next experiment: With a limited budget and only one data point, the highest-value question is whether the second modality is worth pursuing at all. A positive result justifies investing further in image encoder choice, aggregation, and fusion; a null or negative result redirects effort toward RNA encoder variants and profile settings. Choosing the strongest available image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) maximizes the chance of detecting a true benefit, and concat is the simplest fusion, avoiding confounding from learned weighting."
}

